%% -*- mode: erlang -*-
%% Scaffold a complete mcl service: OTP release, container image, CI, and a
%% deployable compose file.
%%
%% THIS EXISTS SO A NEW SERVICE STARTS DEPLOYABLE RATHER THAN STARTING EMPTY.
%% The dull half of a service (release packaging, image, CI, health wiring, the
%% six-callback contract) is the half that is tedious to retrofit and easy to get
%% subtly wrong. Generating it means the first commit of a new service already
%% builds, already passes its own tests, and already has somewhere to run.
%%
%% IT GENERATES NO TODO AND NO STUB. What it emits is honestly complete and
%% empty: the supervisor has no children, the service announces no capability and
%% requests no authority. Those are correct answers for a service that does
%% nothing yet, and each one is asserted by a generated test, so filling them in
%% is a deliberate act that breaks a test rather than a comment someone forgets.
%%
%% TWO NAMES, DELIBERATELY, because they differ and the difference is load
%% bearing. `name' is the OTP application and every module prefix, so it must be
%% a valid Erlang atom in snake_case. `repo' is the git repository, the container
%% image and the name this service answers to on the mesh, and the house
%% convention there is kebab-case. A generated test asserts the two agree modulo
%% the separator, so a mismatched pair fails the first time eunit runs rather
%% than shipping a service whose image and application disagree.
%%
%% Usage, from the directory that will hold the new repository:
%%
%%   rebar3 new mcl_service repo=mcl-foo name=mcl_foo \
%%       desc="Does X over the mesh" health_port=8484
%%
%% THE BUILD AND RUNTIME IMAGES ARE NAMED HERE AND ONLY HERE, as the defaults of
%% builder_image and runtime_image below. scripts/scaffold-service.sh passes
%% them only when overridden, and mcl_service_template_SUITE reads them from
%% this file, so moving the fleet's pair is one edit.

{description, "A complete mcl service: release, container, CI, compose, and the six-callback mcl_om_service contract"}.

{variables, [
    {repo, "mcl-newservice",
     "Repository, container image and mesh-facing name. KEBAB-case."},
    {name, "mcl_newservice",
     "OTP application and module prefix. SNAKE_case, must be a valid Erlang atom, and must match `repo' modulo the separator."},
    {desc, "Does something over the mesh",
     "One line describing what the service does. Ends up in info/0, the app.src and the README."},
    {org, "macula-services",
     "Your source-forge organisation or user. Owns the repository URL and the container image namespace. CHANGE THIS if you are not building for the BEAM Campus fleet."},
    {registry, "ghcr.io",
     "Container registry the image is pushed to. ghcr.io pairs with a GitHub org; set it to whatever you publish to."},
    {builder_image, "ghcr.io/macula-io/macula-ci-otp:20260923-1444@sha256:dd2ba6eb858a0eacedf0179300323fe5c6da46fb308d22da0ca8cfcd1f0718dc",
     "Image the release is BUILT in, by the Containerfile's first stage, and the image lint runs in. Pin it by digest. It must carry OTP 28.4.3 with an OpenSSL that has ML-DSA (the build refuses any other), rebar3, Rust (macula's NIFs always build from source), a C toolchain and git. The default is the macula-services fleet's build image; CHANGE THIS together with runtime_image if you are not building for that fleet."},
    {runtime_image, "ghcr.io/macula-io/macula-pq-runtime:20260923-1444@sha256:15a5501b7277804c5a62c93121d157773d1401d238a1bf630ef4b50fc2f1df09",
     "Image the release RUNS on, the Containerfile's last stage. Pin it by digest. It must match builder_image's libc and carry the libraries the release loads (OpenSSL with ML-DSA, libstdc++, ncurses) and curl for the healthcheck: the two images are a PAIR, and move together. The default is the macula-services fleet's runtime image."},
    {health_port, "8484",
     "Port for the /health endpoint. The container uses host networking, because macula stations are AAAA-only and a default bridge cannot reach them, so a port already bound on the host fails SILENTLY. Pick one you know is free."},
    {holder, "Rafael Lefever",
     "Copyright holder, named in LICENSE. CHANGE THIS if you are not building for the BEAM Campus fleet."},
    {proprietary, "",
     "EMPTY FOR APACHE-2.0, 1 FOR PROPRIETARY. A private service carries a proprietary notice in LICENSE and {licenses, [\"Proprietary\"]} in its app.src; a public one is Apache-2.0 in both. scripts/scaffold-service.sh sets it from MCL_VISIBILITY. Like `store', EXACTLY ONE CHARACTER."},
    {runs_on, "ubuntu-latest",
     "The runner CI jobs run on, as it appears after `runs-on:', e.g. [self-hosted, msi00, pq]. NEVER a self-hosted runner for a public repository: a pull request from anyone would run its code on that machine. scripts/scaffold-service.sh picks it from the org and MCL_VISIBILITY."},
    {store, "",
     "OFF BY DEFAULT. Empty means no store, which is what most services want. Set it to 1 and the service opens a reckon-db store called <name>_store: store_id/0 and data_dir/0 are generated, sys.config gains the evoq adapter block without which the node will not boot, the compose file gains a volume, and three boundary guards are generated to keep them in step. WARNING: the value must be EXACTLY ONE CHARACTER, so 1 and not yes. rebar3 passes template variables as strings and mustache iterates a string as a list, so a longer value repeats every generated block once per character and the result does not compile. That is a limitation of the template engine, not a preference."}
]}.

%% Build
{template, "mcl_service/rebar.config",       "{{repo}}/rebar.config"}.
{template, "mcl_service/gitignore",          "{{repo}}/.gitignore"}.
%% Pinned to the SAME OTP release (28.4.3) the Containerfile's builder stage
%% and lint.yml's toolchain step each refuse anything but.
%% Without this, a dev machine whose asdf/rebar3 global points at a newer
%% OTP (29, in the four repos that hit this in one day) compiles a dependency's deprecated bare
%% `catch' syntax under a version that turns it into a hard build failure
%% via `warnings_as_errors' -- a failure that has nothing to do with the
%% generated service's own code, and reproduces nowhere the pin is honored
%% (CI, the container build, or a machine using this file).
{template, "mcl_service/tool-versions",      "{{repo}}/.tool-versions"}.

%% The application
{template, "mcl_service/app.src",            "{{repo}}/apps/{{name}}/src/{{name}}.app.src"}.
{template, "mcl_service/app.erl",            "{{repo}}/apps/{{name}}/src/{{name}}_app.erl"}.
{template, "mcl_service/sup.erl",            "{{repo}}/apps/{{name}}/src/{{name}}_sup.erl"}.
{template, "mcl_service/service.erl",        "{{repo}}/apps/{{name}}/src/{{name}}_service.erl"}.
{template, "mcl_service/service_tests.erl",  "{{repo}}/apps/{{name}}/test/{{name}}_service_tests.erl"}.

%% Release configuration
{template, "mcl_service/sys.config.src",     "{{repo}}/config/sys.config.src"}.
{template, "mcl_service/vm.args.src",        "{{repo}}/config/vm.args.src"}.

%% Image, CI and deployment
{template, "mcl_service/Containerfile",      "{{repo}}/Containerfile"}.
{template, "mcl_service/build-push.yml",     "{{repo}}/.github/workflows/build-push.yml"}.
{template, "mcl_service/lint.yml",           "{{repo}}/.github/workflows/lint.yml"}.
{template, "mcl_service/compose.yml",        "{{repo}}/deploy/docker-compose.yml"}.

%% Scripts
{template, "mcl_service/health.sh",          "{{repo}}/scripts/health.sh"}.
{chmod,                                         "{{repo}}/scripts/health.sh", 8#755}.
{template, "mcl_service/is_image_push.sh",    "{{repo}}/scripts/is_image_push.sh"}.
{chmod,                                         "{{repo}}/scripts/is_image_push.sh", 8#755}.

%% Documentation
{template, "mcl_service/README.md",          "{{repo}}/README.md"}.
{template, "mcl_service/CHANGELOG.md",       "{{repo}}/CHANGELOG.md"}.
{template, "mcl_service/LICENSE",            "{{repo}}/LICENSE"}.
